WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.026
♪Note: Pyorinland is referring to
Sanrio's Puroland at Tamacenter

00:01.050 --> 00:02.429
Astral Warrior Sunred.

00:02.430 --> 00:04.710
His weapon of choice is a
gun known as "Sunshoot."

00:04.950 --> 00:05.950
Sunshoot!

00:06.930 --> 00:11.040
Sunshoot is a trusty companion that can
easily defeat combat goons in one shot.

00:12.100 --> 00:13.300
So, Mr. Red?

00:13.720 --> 00:15.060
Where's the Sunshoot now?

00:15.510 --> 00:16.510
Who knows.

00:16.690 --> 00:19.990
A couple years back, I think I
kept it in the hardware toolbox.

01:56.630 --> 01:57.880
That's no good!

01:58.250 --> 01:59.250
What was that?

01:59.660 --> 02:02.740
To be frank, I wasn't scared one bit.

02:03.450 --> 02:05.620
I can tell you're not even trying.

02:05.840 --> 02:07.926
There's no way the customers
will appreciate that kind of effort.

02:07.950 --> 02:09.510
Keep practicing until you get it right.

02:09.760 --> 02:10.240
Next!

02:10.450 --> 02:11.190
Your turn, Kimura.

02:11.410 --> 02:11.790
Okay.

02:12.380 --> 02:13.960
Somebody got told.

02:14.100 --> 02:15.460
Shut up.

02:15.650 --> 02:16.769
I'm getting nervous!

02:16.770 --> 02:17.740
Boo!

02:17.200 --> 02:18.920
That wasn't scary at all, he said.

02:19.030 --> 02:21.289
Shut up or I'll curse you!

02:21.290 --> 02:22.820
You try it next, Usakotsu.

02:22.930 --> 02:23.930
O-Okay!

02:24.270 --> 02:25.400
RAWR!

02:27.550 --> 02:30.419
Why are you spreading love all around
when you're supposed to be scaring people?

02:30.420 --> 02:32.300
I did no such thing!

02:32.470 --> 02:37.189
Wouldn't getting a job at Pyorinland
work out better for you than working here?

02:37.190 --> 02:38.636
I'm talking about the one at Tamacenter!

02:38.660 --> 02:40.330
Anyway, keep practicing!

02:40.790 --> 02:42.269
You're up next, Sawada.

02:42.270 --> 02:43.590
The nerve of that guy...

02:44.550 --> 02:45.910
And it trots back to place.

02:46.170 --> 02:48.299
You really are cute, Usakotsu.

02:48.300 --> 02:50.380
I'm not cute!

02:50.490 --> 02:53.469
You're all cute and spongy and stuff.

02:53.470 --> 02:55.929
You look just like the
mascot from Pyorinland.

02:55.930 --> 02:58.620
For being cute, you get
the tickling punishment!

03:01.800 --> 03:03.090
You're both dead meat!

03:03.190 --> 03:04.370
Demon Claw!

03:04.530 --> 03:05.560
What are you guys doing?

03:06.470 --> 03:08.239
Can't you see everyone
else is rehearsing their parts?

03:08.240 --> 03:09.590
We're all working here!

03:10.240 --> 03:12.199
It may only be a part-time job,
but you're getting paid at the end,

03:12.200 --> 03:13.200
so act professional!

03:15.770 --> 03:17.160
You're next, Tanaka.

03:17.980 --> 03:20.570
Isn't he working part-time too?

03:20.730 --> 03:22.070
I'm gonna curse him!

03:22.340 --> 03:23.310
I'll melt that punk!

03:23.311 --> 03:27.570
"You're getting paid, so
act professional" my ass!

03:28.770 --> 03:30.420
That was way off.

03:30.421 --> 03:32.075
I guess a job is a job though...

03:32.076 --> 03:34.660
You should quit while you're
ahead with these things.

03:35.030 --> 03:36.030
But man,

03:37.520 --> 03:40.280
every time I think about what's
going on back at the base...

03:41.240 --> 03:43.521
This is at least two times
more than what we usually pay!

03:43.690 --> 03:46.220
It's a good thing that HQ
sent us an AC they used to use,

03:46.540 --> 03:48.999
but it wastes way too much
energy because it's old.

03:49.000 --> 03:51.440
I can't move a single step.

03:51.860 --> 03:53.229
Does anyone want more barley tea?

03:53.230 --> 03:54.230
Yes, please.

03:54.630 --> 03:55.000
I'll get it.

03:55.310 --> 03:57.260
Don't worry, I'll do it.

03:59.490 --> 04:02.220
If you think about our
electricity bill over at the base...

04:02.360 --> 04:03.360
Yeah.

04:03.550 --> 04:04.930
We have to suck it up!

04:06.870 --> 04:09.460
It's been two weeks
since we started this job.

04:10.900 --> 04:13.020
It was really hard

04:13.710 --> 04:16.359
to get used to things

04:16.360 --> 04:19.419
and become ghosts,

04:19.420 --> 04:21.990
but now we've gotten the hang of it.

04:22.590 --> 04:24.979
Thank you for visiting
Yomiyomiland today...

04:24.980 --> 04:27.909
It was hotter than usual today, wasn't it?

04:27.910 --> 04:29.959
I'd say the heat's starting to get to me.

04:29.960 --> 04:32.350
They really shouldn't make
us wear masks in this weather.

04:33.520 --> 04:34.210
Good job you guys.

04:34.520 --> 04:37.260
Ah, thanks for your troubles, Mr. Satonaka.

04:37.840 --> 04:41.529
We've gone through a
lot together, haven't we?

04:41.530 --> 04:43.699
It's all thanks to you.

04:43.700 --> 04:44.700
Yeah.

04:45.300 --> 04:47.910
We've still got a lot to learn
from your Dracula act, you know.

04:48.040 --> 04:51.320
Let's keep this up until the haunted
house closes down in two weeks!

04:52.000 --> 04:53.630
Well, about that...

04:55.170 --> 04:57.560
Today's my last day working here.

04:59.520 --> 05:00.520
Are you quitting?

05:00.940 --> 05:01.940
Mr. Satonaka...

05:02.130 --> 05:03.130
Now I'm bummed.

05:03.440 --> 05:05.360
My grandpa's having some
money issues right now.

05:05.770 --> 05:07.390
Money issues... I see.

05:08.220 --> 05:10.149
But now's not the time to be bummed!

05:10.150 --> 05:11.870
There's a new job waiting for you tomorrow.

05:12.650 --> 05:16.430
Educate them well, Khamenman!

05:17.150 --> 05:21.210
It may only be a part-time job, but you're
getting paid, so act professional, okay?

05:21.350 --> 05:23.019
Like he's one to talk.

05:23.020 --> 05:24.129
A job's a job, man.

05:24.130 --> 05:26.169
What do you punks think you're doing?

05:26.170 --> 05:28.589
If you have time to chit-chat, think
about how you can be better ghosts!

05:28.590 --> 05:31.220
Be more aware of the
fact that we're working here!

05:31.460 --> 05:33.250
The mummy hunter actually became a mummy.

05:33.970 --> 05:35.970
He was always a mummy to start with.

05:47.180 --> 05:49.480
That yakisoba I had for lunch...

06:08.570 --> 06:09.570
I'm home.

06:10.130 --> 06:11.360
Huh? What are you doing?

06:12.710 --> 06:14.090
Oh, cleaning.

06:16.360 --> 06:17.809
Kayoko's payday.

06:17.810 --> 06:21.860
Astro Fighter Sunred will frequently clean the
house to prove his worth as a you-know-what.

06:25.330 --> 06:27.620
General Vamp's Quick Recipes!

06:28.040 --> 06:29.980
Hi everyone, Vamp here.

06:30.510 --> 06:32.460
Let's get cooking!

06:33.590 --> 06:36.709
Today's menu is super simple.

06:36.710 --> 06:38.929
Kimchi and jyako stir-fry!

06:38.930 --> 06:40.849
These are the ingredients you'll need:

06:40.850 --> 06:42.079
First we need some kimchi,

06:42.080 --> 06:43.219
some jyako,

06:43.220 --> 06:44.769
a little bit of sesame oil,

06:44.770 --> 06:47.440
about a mug full of water...

06:47.830 --> 06:50.120
and there you have the ingredients.

06:50.710 --> 06:52.530
Now let's get to the cooking part.

06:53.080 --> 06:55.460
First, fry the jyako in sesame oil.

06:56.340 --> 07:00.440
Once the jyako is covered in oil,
dump the kimchi in and fry it some more.

07:01.320 --> 07:03.389
Here comes the climax!

07:03.390 --> 07:05.789
I can smell something delicious now!

07:05.790 --> 07:07.079
When you've fried it a good amount,

07:07.080 --> 07:09.080
add water into the mix
and bring it to a boil.

07:10.680 --> 07:12.420
Once it's all nice and boiled...

07:13.690 --> 07:14.700
You're done!

07:14.980 --> 07:17.499
The kimchi and jyako stir-fry is now ready.

07:17.500 --> 07:18.929
You can also try adding some spring onions

07:18.930 --> 07:20.690
and more sesame oil
depending on your taste.

07:22.400 --> 07:23.739
This will make an excellent side dish!

07:23.740 --> 07:27.959
They say if you fry kimchi the right way, a
chemical reaction happens and boost its flavor.

07:27.960 --> 07:29.309
I'd expected no less from you, Vamp.

07:29.310 --> 07:31.110
I'm going to get him to
make some for me too.

07:38.980 --> 07:40.380
Good morning, Mr. Akiyama.

07:41.790 --> 07:43.170
Ah, morning Pdora.

07:43.720 --> 07:44.929
You're drenched.

07:44.930 --> 07:46.400
Well I can't be late.

07:47.500 --> 07:49.179
Where's Mr. Taguchi?

07:49.180 --> 07:49.820
He went to the bank.

07:50.190 --> 07:51.190
I'm back.

07:51.430 --> 07:53.419
Ah, good morning Mr. Taguchi.

07:53.420 --> 07:54.420
Morning.

07:54.930 --> 07:55.949
Let's get going.

07:55.950 --> 07:57.990
I'll go buy our tickets.

07:59.630 --> 08:01.509
So that's the guy you want to scout?

08:01.510 --> 08:02.350
Yes, sir.

08:02.351 --> 08:04.339
He's got to be a Pteranodon.

08:04.340 --> 08:05.340
No doubt.

08:08.900 --> 08:10.109
I wonder where he's headed.

08:10.110 --> 08:10.960
To the job site.

08:10.961 --> 08:12.219
He's part-timing, apparently.

08:12.220 --> 08:13.130
They're leaving.

08:13.130 --> 08:14.130
Let's follow them!

08:18.190 --> 08:19.190
Kita-senju?

08:19.560 --> 08:21.070
All right, keep still.

08:22.510 --> 08:23.520
Okay, that's good.

08:23.860 --> 08:24.370
Let's move to the next spot.

08:24.580 --> 08:25.580
Yes, sir.

08:25.980 --> 08:27.500
They're surveying the Kita-senju area.

08:28.060 --> 08:28.570
Let's move to the next spot.

08:28.730 --> 08:28.960
Yes, sir.

08:29.560 --> 08:31.209
Surveying the Kita-senju area.

08:31.210 --> 08:31.750
Next.

08:31.750 --> 08:32.190
Yes, sir!

08:32.191 --> 08:33.979
Surveying the Kita-senju area.

08:33.980 --> 08:34.580
Next.

08:34.580 --> 08:34.860
Yes, sir!

08:35.440 --> 08:37.000
He sure is enthusiastic about his work.

08:37.350 --> 08:38.540
He's a hard worker.

08:39.540 --> 08:41.379
I think this pen's out of ink.

08:41.380 --> 08:43.449
I'll go to the convenience
store and get you a new one.

08:43.450 --> 08:45.540
I have another one, don't worry.

08:46.180 --> 08:48.010
You should calm down a bit, Pdora.

08:48.670 --> 08:49.670
I'm sorry.

08:59.090 --> 09:01.639
I'll go get you more water Mr. Akiyama.

09:01.640 --> 09:02.270
Thanks.

09:02.270 --> 09:03.336
Would you like more water too, Mr. Taguchi?

09:03.360 --> 09:04.360
Yes, please.

09:05.940 --> 09:07.949
He sure is polite isn't he?

09:07.950 --> 09:08.950
Yeah.

09:09.470 --> 09:11.390
Do you mind if I walk around a little?

09:11.720 --> 09:13.500
Yeah, let's break 'til one.

09:13.610 --> 09:14.610
Okay.

09:18.110 --> 09:19.230
I guess I'll get some juice.

09:20.030 --> 09:21.519
Now's the chance, Master Vamp!

09:21.520 --> 09:22.750
You're right, let's go.

09:24.810 --> 09:26.800
Who are you guys?

09:27.760 --> 09:31.210
Don't worry, we're not
strange people or anything.

09:32.780 --> 09:34.470
I guess I was right then.

09:34.990 --> 09:37.940
So your mom was a Pteranodon.

09:38.250 --> 09:38.830
Yeah.

09:38.831 --> 09:41.359
He does look exactly like
the ones in the picture book.

09:41.360 --> 09:43.709
I think I saw them in
Jurassic Parking as well...

09:43.710 --> 09:44.440
I think it was the third one?

09:44.440 --> 09:45.100
Um...

09:45.101 --> 09:49.039
Did you know that Pteranodons are
actually pterosaurs, not dinosaurs?

09:49.040 --> 09:49.900
Oh, really?

09:49.700 --> 09:50.700
Excuse me!

09:50.930 --> 09:53.110
Is that why you called me over?

09:54.670 --> 09:56.660
Oh, no, sorry.

09:57.980 --> 10:00.770
Actually, how should I put it...

10:01.170 --> 10:04.489
It might sound a bit sudden for me ask but,

10:04.490 --> 10:07.410
are you interested in world
domination at all, Pdora?

10:08.130 --> 10:09.620
World domination?

10:10.060 --> 10:11.830
Taking over the world...

10:12.180 --> 10:14.590
Are you interested at all?

10:15.570 --> 10:16.340
Are you?

10:16.340 --> 10:17.340
Well...

10:17.410 --> 10:18.070
Maybe a little?

10:18.071 --> 10:20.180
Wait a second here!

10:20.670 --> 10:24.590
I've never even thought
about world domination before.

10:25.470 --> 10:26.590
So asking me isn't really...

10:27.290 --> 10:28.629
That's all right then.

10:28.630 --> 10:30.769
Oh yeah, it's perfectly fine.

10:30.770 --> 10:32.660
You don't have to give
us an answer right away.

10:34.600 --> 10:41.539
Well actually, I don't think world
domination is going to be that easy either.

10:41.540 --> 10:42.780
Honestly speaking anyway.

10:43.130 --> 10:46.900
I... just want to actually make it happen.

10:47.030 --> 10:47.280
Yeah.

10:47.810 --> 10:51.820
Our goal at hand is to take down
Sunred for the time being though.

10:52.020 --> 10:53.060
But you know,

10:53.890 --> 10:56.029
if we take down Sunred, then...

10:56.030 --> 10:57.939
We'll be...

10:57.940 --> 10:59.929
Oh that's right, we'll
be getting somewhere.

10:59.930 --> 11:00.930
For sure.

11:01.150 --> 11:02.350
But I...

11:03.250 --> 11:05.475
I know you're attending night school,

11:05.476 --> 11:06.890
Welcome!

11:05.940 --> 11:07.960
But we can adjust to your schedule.

11:08.970 --> 11:10.210
There you are, Pdora.

11:11.170 --> 11:12.170
Is it time to go already?

11:13.390 --> 11:14.390
Who are these guys?

11:15.390 --> 11:18.049
What are you doing to our young talent?

11:18.050 --> 11:19.519
Are you trying to get him
mixed up in something here?

11:19.520 --> 11:20.969
No, we're not.

11:20.970 --> 11:23.979
You're one of those
get-rich-quick schemers, aren't you?

11:23.980 --> 11:26.849
They're not trying to get me
involved anything bad, I swear.

11:26.850 --> 11:29.049
They're not strange people!
